{
	"_doc": "People of Night City (People.roll / People.types): who a client, an assassination mark or a rescue captive is. A d10 picks the zone (Corporate/Upscale 1-3, Moderate/Community 4-6, Street/Combat Zone 7-9, Outskirts 10), then the zone's die picks a type of person. Schema: zones.<id> = {name, zone_roll [lo, hi] on the d10, die ('1d10' or '2d10'), cite, types: [{id, label, roll [lo, hi] on the zone's die, kind}]}. `label` is a short paraphrased role label (lower case, reads after 'a'/'an'); `kind` is a coarse tag for other systems: corp, civic, street, crime, media, tech, medic, nomad, ai, kin. Table structure and entries from R. Talsorian's Cyberpunk RED: Single Player Mode, printed p.50-51 (paraphrased labels only, no book text).",
